WEBVTT

00:00:00.256 --> 00:00:02.744
A new cluster needs more than an installer.

00:00:02.816 --> 00:00:07.168
Its physical nodes need approved images and addresses, its services need

00:00:07.168 --> 00:00:11.021
configuration, and its recovery process needs a reviewed plan.

00:00:11.136 --> 00:00:15.181
ZTF Orchestrator brings those activities into one browser console.

00:00:15.360 --> 00:00:17.954
This walkthrough follows a simulated Cluster A;

00:00:18.005 --> 00:00:19.953
it changes no infrastructure.

00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:24.463
The Orchestrator stores reviewed YAML, credential references, approvals

00:00:24.557 --> 00:00:28.602
and job evidence. ZTF one point x remains the workflow

00:00:28.610 --> 00:00:30.074
and pipeline executor.

00:00:30.189 --> 00:00:33.668
Foundation VM performs the imaging and cluster formation.

00:00:33.878 --> 00:00:38.052
Prism and guarded specialist adapters perform their supported target actions.

00:00:38.358 --> 00:00:40.484
The Orchestrator coordinates those systems;

00:00:40.534 --> 00:00:42.326
it does not replace Foundation.

00:00:42.649 --> 00:00:46.950
Start Here offers deployment, configuration, recovery, monitoring

00:00:46.958 --> 00:00:51.046
and saved automation. YAML Studio helps prepare a configuration

00:00:51.225 --> 00:00:52.817
and hand it to a pipeline.

00:00:52.974 --> 00:00:55.105
Saving a file starts no job.

00:00:55.247 --> 00:00:59.386
Successful authoring checks do not prove that a password works or that a target is

00:00:59.386 --> 00:01:03.794
ready. Recovery profiles preserve deployment and pipeline snapshots.

00:01:03.951 --> 00:01:07.942
Resume an existing recovery to retain approvals and completed work.

00:01:08.151 --> 00:01:12.196
Monitoring distinguishes recorded health, failed collection and expired

00:01:12.247 --> 00:01:16.250
evidence. Inspect the result behind a status before accepting the cluster

00:01:16.386 --> 00:01:19.186
for workload restoration through your backup platform.

00:01:19.391 --> 00:01:23.999
Native pipeline opt-in, NKP and ZTF two point x console

00:01:23.999 --> 00:01:25.590
execution are retired.

00:01:25.748 --> 00:01:27.340
Historical records remain.

00:01:27.540 --> 00:01:31.171
Specialist changes keep their own approval and verification gates.

00:01:31.404 --> 00:01:35.628
This release is a candidate, and simulated videos do not establish hardware

00:01:35.628 --> 00:01:39.710
compatibility. Begin with Start Here and the current written guide.
